    $buildMarkerLines += '2244: OOBE delivery bootstrap stale-lock fix + HKLM Run -> bootstrap redirect. Root cause: bootstrap lock left from killed OOBE defaultuser0 session blocked Active Setup / Startup re-delivery; HKLM Run bypassed bootstrap and fired at real-user logon. Fix: stale-lock detection in FirstBaseOobeDeferredSoundBootstrap.ps1 (clears dead-pid lock and retries); Register-FbDeferredOobeSoundHklmRunFallback now points to bootstrap (not deferred sound directly) so all paths go through stale-lock-aware bootstrap. FirstBasePostSysprepOobeSoundArm.ps1 HKLM Run fallback also updated to bootstrap path. SB safety net in FirstBaseOobeOperatorFinalize.ps1: Confirm-SecureBootUEFI check before shutdown; redirects to /fw if SB disabled.'
    $buildMarkerLines += '2247: DeferredOobeSoundOnLogon ONLOGON task created inline in STAGE 2 handoff (post-scrub, pre-sysprep). Root cause: detached arm worker (FirstBasePostSysprepOobeSoundArm.ps1) runs after sysprep.exe exits, at which point Task Scheduler COM server is gone (exit -2147467259 / 0x80004005 E_FAIL); 2245 SetupComplete.cmd fix ineffective because Bug NN / 2213t deletes SetupComplete.cmd before sysprep. Fix: Register-FbDeferredOobeSoundOnLogonTaskPreSysprep called in Invoke-FbOobeHandoff STAGE 2 after Invoke-FbPreSysprepScrub returns and before Invoke-SysprepToOobe; task XML at C:\Windows\System32\Tasks\FirstBase\DeferredOobeSoundOnLogon survives generalize; Task Scheduler re-registers from XML on OOBE boot; task fires for defaultuser0 at logon. Invoke-FbPreSysprepScrub STEP 2 unconditionally excludes DeferredOobeSoundOnLogon from its delete set.'
